    "gold_solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom gurobipy import *\n\ndef solve_problem():\n    m = Model(\"VRPTW\")\n    m.setParam('TimeLimit', 300)\n\n    # --- Data ---\n    n_customers = 5\n    n_vehicles = 4\n    Q = 48  # vehicle capacity\n    vehicle_fixed_cost = 100.0\n    depot = [50, 50]\n    customers = [[21, 65], [46, 67], [42, 26], [69, 82], [48, 61]]\n    demands = [24, 11, 13, 12, 7]\n    time_windows = [[0, 276], [44, 98], [36, 116], [39, 124], [33, 96], [27, 113]]\n    service_times = [7, 13, 12, 12, 15]\n\n    # Node 0 = depot, nodes 1..N = customers\n    N = n_customers\n    nodes = list(range(N + 1))\n    cust_nodes = list(range(1, N + 1))\n\n    # Coordinates: index 0 = depot, 1..N = customers\n    coords = [depot] + customers\n\n    # COMPUTE distance matrix from coordinates\n    dist = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                dist[(i,j)] = math.sqrt(\n                    (coords[i][0]-coords[j][0])**2 +\n                    (coords[i][1]-coords[j][1])**2)\n\n    # Service time by node (depot = 0)\n    svc = [0] + service_times\n\n    # Big-M for time linking\n    T_max = time_windows[0][1]\n    max_svc = max(service_times)\n    max_dist = max(dist.values())\n    M = T_max + max_svc + max_dist + 1\n\n    # --- Variables ---\n    # Arc variables (binary)\n    x = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        for j in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                x[(i,j)] = m.addVar(vtype=GRB.BINARY, name=f\"Arc_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # Load variables (MTZ subtour elimination)\n    u = {}\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        u[i] = m.addVar(lb=demands[i-1], ub=Q, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Load_{i}\")\n\n    # Time variables\n    t = {}\n    for i in nodes:\n        a, b = time_windows[i]\n        t[i] = m.addVar(lb=a, ub=b, vtype=GRB.CONTINUOUS, name=f\"Time_{i}\")\n    # Fix depot departure to time 0\n    t[0].ub = 0.0\n\n    # --- Objective ---\n    # Minimize travel distance + vehicle fixed costs\n    obj = quicksum(dist[(i,j)] * x[(i,j)] for i in nodes for j in nodes if i != j)\n    obj += quicksum(vehicle_fixed_cost * x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes)\n    m.setObjective(obj, GRB.MINIMIZE)\n\n    # --- Constraints ---\n    # 1. Each customer has exactly one outgoing arc\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for j in nodes if j != i) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitOut_C{i}\")\n\n    # 2. Each customer has exactly one incoming arc\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        m.addConstr(\n            quicksum(x[(i,j)] for i in nodes if i != j) == 1,\n            name=f\"VisitIn_C{j}\")\n\n    # 3. At most K vehicles leave the depot\n    m.addConstr(\n        quicksum(x[(0,j)] for j in cust_nodes) <= n_vehicles,\n        name=\"VehicleLimit\")\n\n    # 4. MTZ subtour elimination\n    for i in cust_nodes:\n        for j in cust_nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    u[i] - u[j] + Q * x[(i,j)] <= Q - demands[j-1],\n                    name=f\"MTZ_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    # 5. Time linking: if arc (i,j) is used, arrival at j >= departure from i\n    for j in cust_nodes:\n        for i in nodes:\n            if i != j:\n                m.addConstr(\n                    t[i] - t[j] + M * x[(i,j)] <= M - svc[i] - dist[(i,j)],\n                    name=f\"TimeLink_{i}_{j}\")\n\n    m.optimize()\n    return m\n```",
    "LLM_description": "To: Distribution Planning Team\nFrom: Logistics Operations Manager\nSubject: Routing and Scheduling Requirements for Single-Trip Deliveries from Central Depot\nDate: [Today]\n\nOverview\nWe will execute a next-day delivery plan from a single central depot using a small fleet of identical vehicles. The operation entails visiting a defined set of customer locations and returning to the depot within the same planning horizon. All vehicles will depart the depot at time 0, complete a single trip each, and return before the depot\u2019s latest return time.\n\nRouting and Scheduling Challenge\n- Each vehicle must leave the depot at time 0, visit a sequence of assigned customers, and return to the depot before the depot closing time. No vehicle is permitted to run multiple tours or reload during the horizon.\n- Every customer must be visited exactly once by exactly one vehicle.\n- The plan must specify a feasible visit order for each vehicle and the corresponding schedule at each stop, including any waiting time if arrival occurs before a customer\u2019s earliest service time.\n\nOperating Rules and Service Requirements\n- Time windows:\n  - Each customer provides an earliest and latest acceptable start-of-service time.\n  - If a vehicle arrives early, it must wait until the window opens. Service must begin within the stated window.\n- Service times:\n  - Each customer has a defined unloading/service duration. After service is complete, the vehicle departs immediately. If the vehicle had to wait for the window to open, departure occurs after window_open + service_time; otherwise, after arrival_time + service_time.\n- Capacity:\n  - Vehicles are identical and capacity-limited. The total demand of all customers assigned to a vehicle must not exceed that vehicle\u2019s capacity at any point along its route.\n- Travel time and distance:\n  - Travel time between any two locations equals the straight-line distance between their coordinates, with an implicit speed of 1. Distance units equal time units.\n  - All routes start and end at the depot.\n\nCost Structure and Goal\n- Each deployed vehicle incurs a fixed cost, in addition to the distance-related cost of travel. The plan may use fewer than the maximum number of vehicles where feasible to reduce fixed costs.\n- Goal: Identify a set of single-trip routes that visits every customer exactly once, respects all time windows and service durations, stays within vehicle capacity limits, and minimizes the total travel distance plus vehicle deployment costs.\n\nDeliverables\n- For each vehicle: ordered customer sequence, planned arrival times, any waiting times, service start and end times, and depot return time.\n- Confirmation that all customers are served exactly once and that all capacity and timing constraints are satisfied within the planning horizon.\n\nANNEX \u2013 Operations Data\n- Depot location (coordinates): (50, 50)\n- Depot latest return time (planning horizon end): 276\n- Customer locations (coordinates): Customer Locations (coordinates):\n  - C1: (21, 65)\n  - C2: (46, 67)\n  - C3: (42, 26)\n  - C4: (69, 82)\n  - C5: (48, 61)\n- Customer delivery time windows: Customer Time Windows [earliest, latest]:\n  - C1: [44, 98]\n  - C2: [36, 116]\n  - C3: [39, 124]\n  - C4: [33, 96]\n  - C5: [27, 113]\n- Customer service times (unloading durations): Service Times (minutes at customer):\n  - C1: 7\n  - C2: 13\n  - C3: 12\n  - C4: 12\n  - C5: 15\n- Customer demands (units): Customer Demands:\n  - C1: 24 units\n  - C2: 11 units\n  - C3: 13 units\n  - C4: 12 units\n  - C5: 7 units\n- Number of vehicles available: 4\n- Vehicle capacity (units): 48\n- Fixed deployment cost per vehicle: 100.0",
